7. Create an image of php project and push on Dockerhub repository.
Firstly create a docker folder:
Dockerfile
# Use PHP CLI (Command Line Interface) as the base image
FROM php:8.4-cli

# Copy all files from the current directory to /var/www/html inside the container
COPY . /var/www/html

# Set the working directory
WORKDIR /var/www/html

# Expose port 5000 for accessing the application
EXPOSE 5000

# Start the PHP built-in server on port 5000
CMD ["php", "-S", "0.0.0.0:5000"]

Index.php:

<?php
echo "Hello from Dockerized PHP!";
?>
Save these files in the docker folder.
Open docker desktop:
Open terminal
Cd “file path”
Build the Docker image:
docker build -t yourdockerhubname/php-server .
Run the Docker container on port 5000:
docker run -d -p 5000:5000 yourdockerhubname/php-server

http://localhost:5000
