8. Demonstrate use of docker commands to pull ubuntu official image, create a file and push updated image on Dockerhub.
Great! Here's a full step-by-step demonstration using Docker commands to:
Pull the official Ubuntu image


Create a file inside a running container


Commit the changes as a new image


Push that updated image to Docker Hub



🧱 Step-by-Step Guide

✅ Step 1: Pull the Official Ubuntu Image
docker pull ubuntu


✅ Step 2: Run a Container from Ubuntu Image

docker run -it ubuntu

This will open a shell inside the container. Now run:

apt update
apt install -y nano    # or use touch if nano not needed
echo "Hello from Docker Ubuntu!" > hello.txt
exit

Now you’ve created a hello.txt file inside the container and exited.

✅ Step 3: Get the Container ID

docker ps -a

Note the CONTAINER ID of the one you just exited.

✅ Step 4: Commit the Container as a New Image

docker commit <container-id> yourdockerhubname/ubuntu-with-hello

Example:
docker commit abc1234 yourdockerhubname/ubuntu-with-hello


✅ Step 5: Push the New Image to Docker Hub
Log in to Docker Hub:
docker login

Push your image:

docker push yourdockerhubname/ubuntu-with-hello


✅ To Verify
Anyone can now pull your updated image:

docker pull yourdockerhubname/ubuntu-with-hello
docker run -it yourdockerhubname/ubuntu-with-hello
cat hello.txt
